#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## The digit reader over a batch: the first 1,000 MNIST test digits as
## one batch through the Conv library (the windows of every picture,
## one product for the batch, the pooling), then the dense layer; how
## many digits it reads right, the count the trainer's Rust forward
## pass gives from the same pixels. The batch run for a GPU
## (docs/gpu-asks.md); cnn-digits.xtl is the lesson, a picture at a time.

"nn:" u_se< "NN"
"cv:" u_se< "Conv"

### The network, read from data/ (as cnn-digits.xtl reads it)
fb := 8 10 r_eshape n_umbers []N_GET "data/filters.txt"
wb := 1353 10 r_eshape n_umbers []N_GET "data/dense.txt"

### The batch: the test digits, their pixels as whole percents, and their labels
X := (1000 28 28 r_eshape n_umbers []N_GET "data/test-digits.txt") / 100.0
labels := f_loor n_umbers []N_GET "data/test-labels.txt"

### The reader
## The digit, 0 to 9, the network reads in each picture of a batch X:
## the filters over every window, ReLU, 2 x 2 pooling, the dense layer,
## the likeliest output. One function of arrays, the part a GPU takes.
u:r_ead := { X ->
  (nn:a_rgmax (((t_ally X) c_at 1352) r_eshape cv:p_ool nn:r_elu (9 t_ake_2 fb, r_avel -1 t_ake_2 fb) cv:c_onv X) nn:d_ense wb) - 1
}
# -- end of the core ------------------------------------------

### How many of the 1,000 it reads right, and that the Rust model counts the same
right := f_loor '+ r_/ f_loat (u:r_ead X) = labels
right
right = f_loor n_umbers []N_GET "data/test-right.txt"
